ALGORITHMS
MODULE 1: Slot availability display
START
Connect to the Parking_slots Database
Initialize counter availability = 0
For each slot_no in Parking_slots table DO
      IF slot_status == "FREE" display slot_no, available, slot_zone
        available = available + 1
      ELSE
        display unavailable
      END IF
END FOR 
Display slots available // this dislaays the available slots and their slot_numnber and slot_zone
STOP

MODULE 2: Vehicle Entry
START
Ask for vehicles plate number
IF plate_number.status == 'parked'
    THEN REJECT 'Vehicle already inside'
END IF
IF available == 0
    THEN REJECT 'Parking full'
ELSE 
    Allocate an available slot_no
    Record current date and time
    Record plate number, vehicle type and phone number
    Update slot_status = 'occupied' WHERE slotID = slotID
    Display ticket: plate, vehicle type, phone number, slot, entry time
END IF
STOP

MODULE 3: Slot allocation
START
Build a list free_bays 
IF free_bays == EMPTY  display "PARKING FULL"
ELSE 
  choose slot with lowest slot_no in free_bays
  remove slot from free_bays
  slot == "occupied" // status stored in the Database
END IF
Display slot_id
STOP

MODULE 4: Duration and fee calculation
START
Search vehicle number plate from the records
IF plate_number ='parked'
     THEN retrieve vehicle information, slot and entry time
ELSE 
      Display vehicle not found
END IF
Duration = current time - entry time
IF duration <= 30 min
    fee = 0
ELSE IF duration <= 2 hours
    fee = 50
ELSE IF duration <= 4 hours
    fee = 100
ELSE IF duration <= 6 hours
    fee = 300
ELSE 
    fee = 500
END IF
Display duration
Display fee
STOP

MODULE 5: Payment collection
START
Connect to the Payment table
IF amount_due = 0 THEN display payment as  "FREE_EXIT" //When parking duration <=30 minutes
   returen payment confirmed and barriar is opened
END IF
  ELSE IF payment method = M-PESA:
     send a STK push to driver's phone //DARAJA_STK_PUSH
     wait for confirmation
 ELSE IF payment method = CARD:
     charge the card 
     IF amount available in CARD < amount_due return payment rejected //barrier reemains closed
        ELSE
         wait for approval
      END IF
 ELSE IF payment method = CASH:
      the attendant enters cash received
      IF cash < amount_due return payment rejected
    ELSE
      cash > anount_due give change
  END IF
END IF
When payment is not confirmed return payment rejected
Save  payment to  the Payments table // in the Database
STOP

MODULE 6: Exit Barrier Control
START
Check payment status
IF payment status == 'Confirmed'
     Open Barrier
     Record exit time
     Update vehicle status to 'exited'
     Update slot_status to 'free'
ELSE
    Keep barrier closed
    Display 'Payment required'
END IF
STOP

MODULE 7:Admin and reporting
START
Select SUM(amount_paid) FROM payments WHERE DATE(timestamp) of the date selected
Group by payment_method
Select COUNT(*) FROM vehichles WHERE DATE(entry_time) of the date selected
Display the revenue per payment method, total vehichles, occupancy rates
STOP

DATA STRUCTURES AND THEIT JUSTIFICATION
1.Array
   Where used and justification:
     Used for the in-memory copy of parking slots loaded from the Parking_slots table at start-up.
     Slots are fixed and numbered, giving direct index access, which makes it easy to render the 
     visual grid the client asked for — no shifting of elements is needed when a slot's status 
     changes. Also used for the fee schedule loaded from Tariffs: a small, fixed set of bands 
     that is scanned once per lookup, kept dynamic by loading from the table rather than 
     hard-coding values in code.
2. Hash Table/Map
   Where used and justification:
    a. Used in active tickets looked up by the ticker ID for a avarage lookup at the exit with  
       no scanning through records. This is essential in the working of the barrier.
    b. In the plate ID number through the ticket ID index so that drivers are identified by plate 
       and not ID in an instant mapping the plate to the ticket.
3.Queue
   Where used and justification:
    Used when there are waiting drivers when the parking is fully occupied by ensuring that the 
    first driver to arrive enters first when a slot frees (FIFO is fair). It supports "parking
    full" scenario.
4.Linked list
   Where used and justification:
    Used in the archive of exited vehicles where the  unkown,growing size is stored in the dynamic 
    memory  and an insert is used at the front making it ideal for "recent exits" reports (newest first).
 5.Stack  
    Where use and justification:
     Undoes the user (admim or attendant) action and the processing of ticket print jobs based on 
     the last in first out ensuring the last action is reserved first. 
    